## Sugar (sucrose)
component-sucrose = Sugar (sucrose)
    .genitive = sugar
component-sucrose-decomposes-into = caramel, water and then carbon (it chars)
component-sucrose-description-novice = Ordinary sugar. It dissolves extremely well in water — a glass of water can dissolve twice its own mass of sugar. Heated, it does not simply melt but caramelises and chars.
component-sucrose-description-school = Unlike salt, sugar does not split into ions in water, so a sugar solution does not conduct electricity. Its solubility rises strongly with temperature — that is how syrups are made and sugar crystals grown.
component-sucrose-model-notes = The enthalpy of solution is not checked against sources yet, so in the model dissolving does not change the temperature.
